# The Z3817A's 1 PPS divider, stop and sync blocks, each the Z3805A's
# (z3817a-trace.md, "The 1 PPS divider", "Start, stop and status bits"
# and "The sync field"), checked by `make -f tools/fpga/Makefile
# check-blocks` (blockmatch.py).  The blocks sit in other tiles, and
# many of them use their two flip-flops the other way round, so most
# pairs name two tiles and rename the outputs.
#
# The prescaler: JA, the Z3805A's GI, its flip-flops exchanged; JB, its
# terminal, GI's HI.
pair JA GI
rename JA.QX GI.QY
rename JA.QY GI.QX
rename JA.X GI.Y
rename JA.Y GI.X
pair JB HI
rename JB.X HI.Y
# The 6-bit counter of 156 or 157 clocks: IC, KC, JC and ID, the
# Z3805A's IG, JH, IH and JI, IC's and ID's flip-flops exchanged; JD,
# the Z3805A's II.  ID's terminal reads HC.X, the prescaler's step, where
# JI's reads GK.Y; HC is not GK (below).
pair IC IG
rename IC.QX IG.QY
rename IC.QY IG.QX
rename IC.X IG.Y
rename IC.Y IG.X
pair KC JH
pair JC IH
pair ID JI
rename ID.QX JI.QY
rename ID.Y JI.X
pair JD II
rename JD.Y II.X
rename HC.X GK.Y
# The counter's terminal a clock later and the restart's OR: KD, the
# Z3805A's HJ, and LD, its FJ.
pair KD HJ
rename KD.QX HJ.QY
rename KD.X HJ.Y
pair LD FJ
# The divide by 64: FA, GA, FC and GC, the Z3805A's KH, KI, KJ and KK,
# FC's and GC's flip-flops exchanged; FB, KK's carry, its JJ; HD, the
# 10,000-clock enable, its JK.  HD reads GB.Y, which is the Z3805A's
# IJ.X; GB is not IJ (below).
pair FA KH
pair GA KI
pair FC KJ
rename FC.QX KJ.QY
rename FC.X KJ.Y
pair GC KK
rename GC.QX KK.QY
rename GC.X KK.Y
pair FB JJ
pair HD JK
rename GB.Y IJ.X
# The three decades.  GF and GG, the Z3805A's KF and KG, GG's flip-flops
# exchanged, and HF their carry, its JG, its outputs exchanged; FE and
# FF, its GE and GF, FF's flip-flops exchanged; FG, its HF, FG's
# flip-flop and outputs exchanged; FH and GH, its GG and HG.  GH.Y is the
# tap.
pair GF KF
pair GG KG
rename GG.QX KG.QY
rename GG.QY KG.QX
rename GG.X KG.Y
pair HF JG
rename HF.X JG.Y
rename HF.Y JG.X
pair FE GE
pair FF GF
rename FF.QX GF.QY
rename FF.QY GF.QX
rename FF.X GF.Y
pair FG HF
rename FG.QX HF.QY
rename FG.X HF.Y
rename FG.Y HF.X
pair FH GG
pair GH HG
# The terminal count is split here: GD.X is the Z3805A's HH.Y, and GE.X
# is HH.X ORed with IF.Y, kind 3's restart (below).
rename GD.X HH.Y
# The sync field's register, IG, the Z3805A's DI; its copy a clock
# behind, JE, its DJ, JE's flip-flop and outputs exchanged; the restart,
# IF, its EJ; the step lines, HE, its GJ.
pair IG DI
pair JE DJ
rename JE.QX DJ.QY
rename JE.X DJ.Y
rename JE.Y DJ.X
pair IF EJ
pair HE GJ
# What those read from outside them.  CD, the 1 PPS's rising-edge
# detector, the Z3805A's DH, its flip-flops exchanged as the 58503B's
# are: it samples AG.X, the selected 1 PPS, where the Z3805A samples P82
# (PAD15), the same pin with register 4's bit 0 clear.  JF.Y, the
# pending sync, is the Z3805A's EK.X; JF is not EK (below).  IG reads
# EL.X, the register-3 write decode, by its name in both: EL is not
# paired (below).
pair CD DH
rename CD.QX DH.QY
rename CD.QY DH.QX
rename AG.X PAD15.I
rename JF.Y EK.X
# The stop: BJ, clocked by the tap through EH, the Z3805A's CI, clocked
# through GH; DI, the last of its pipeline, the Z3805A's DG.  BJ takes
# BI.X, the start bit, where the Z3805A's CI takes AH.X; LH.X, the
# preset, is the Z3805A's FH.Y.  CI, the pipeline's first stage, is not
# CJ (below).
pair BJ CI
rename EH.Y GH.X
rename BI.X AH.X
rename LH.X FH.Y
pair DI DG
rename CI.Y CJ.Y
# The count's bit 0: BH, the Z3805A's CF, gated by the start, AI.Y,
# read by its name in both (AI is not paired, below), and by the stop,
# DI.Y.
pair BH CF
#
# Not the Z3805A's, and so not paired:
# - GB: its GB.Y is IJ.X, but GB.X is the Z3805A's IJ.Y ORed with HE.X,
#   the kind 1 step, folded in ahead of the prescaler's step logic.
# - HC: the prescaler's step, the Z3805A's GK in another encoding,
#   reading GB.X and HE.Y where GK reads IJ.Y and both step lines.
# - GD and GE: the Z3805A's HH, split in two, GE ORing in IF.Y, so that
#   kind 3's restart makes the internal 1 PPS on the GPS edge, as the
#   Z3816A's does, where the Z3805A's comes a second later.
# - JF and IE: the pending sync, the Z3805A's EK, which the internal
#   1 PPS clears whatever the kind; here IE clears it on the internal
#   1 PPS only for kinds 1 and 2, and on kind 3's restart.
# - EL: its X is the Z3805A's, of the same pads and the write strobe,
#   its Y register 4's write decode, where the Z3805A's EL.Y is register
#   0's (FL.X here); and the strobe is GK.Y, in one block, where the
#   Z3805A's is FL.Y, from FK.
# - The start, BI and AI, and CI: the Z3805A's have the reference bit
#   and the start's pulse, AH; here AH is constant Low, and CI ORs AH.Y
#   where the Z3805A's CJ ORs BH.X.
